<div class="container">
  <h2>This server</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>{@server_name}</strong>
    is a platform for hosting and sharing
    terminal session recordings, powered by
    <%= if @server_version do %>
      <a href="https://github.com/asciinema/asciinema-server">asciinema server</a>
      ({@server_version}).
    <% else %>
      <a href="https://github.com/asciinema/asciinema-server">asciinema server</a>.
    <% end %>
  </p>

  <%= if @contact_email_address do %>
    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      You can reach this server's administrator at
      <strong><.obfuscated_email address={@contact_email_address} /></strong>
      for help with:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>account access problems,</li>
      <li>recording recovery,</li>
      <li>reporting inappropriate content,</li>
      <li>reporting security vulnerabilities.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      For other questions, check the asciinema <a href="https://docs.asciinema.org/faq/">FAQ</a>
      or reach out to the <a href="https://docs.asciinema.org/community/">asciinema community</a>.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <h2>The asciinema project</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>asciinema</strong> is a suite of tools
    for recording, replaying, and sharing terminal sessions. It is free and open-source software, created by <a href="https://hachyderm.io/@ku1ik">Marcin Kulik</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Visit <a href="https://docs.asciinema.org">docs.asciinema.org</a>
    to learn how asciinema works, explore integrations, or set up your own server.
    You can also find ways to get involved in the community and support the project.
  </p>
</div>
